    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "MAY QUALIFY FOR THE VACANT HOME GRANT TO AVAIL OF UP TO €50,000 TOWARDS REFURBISHMENT. FOR FULL DETAILS AND CRITERIA PLEASE SEE: https://www.localgov.ie/grants-and-funding/vacant-property-refurbishment-grant-croi-conaithe-towns-fund\r\n\r\nPresenting an utterly charming two-storey detached residence in a highly sought-after coastal setting, within walking distance of the beautiful white sandy beach at Ballyconnigar, Blackwater, Co. Wexford, set on c 1.36 acre approx. enjoying spectacular sea views of the coastline to the rear and side of the property. \r\nThis most appealing home offers an excellent opportunity as a comfortable year-round residence or a superb holiday retreat, combining generous accommodation with a sensational location close to the coast. The property is ready for its new owners to put their own stamp on and create a home tailored to their taste. View of the beautiful coastline from upstairs bedroom. \r\nAccommodation comprises an entrance porch and welcoming hallway tiled , a cosy sitting room featuring a beautiful stove, kitchen with tiled floor, french door to paved patio area ( concrete floor)  , a practical utility room with fitted units. The ground floor also includes a family bathroom with WC, WHB and bath with mixer shower overhead fully tiled, together with a convenient ground-floor bedroom with laminate timber floor. \r\nUpstairs, there are two further spacious double bedrooms(concrete floor)  and a shower room with wc/whb and shower cubicle , pumped shower also tiled, providing flexible accommodation for family, guests or holiday use.\r\nBuilt in 2005 block-built construction, the property benefits from underfloor heating, solid concrete floors, oil-fired central heating, a recently upgraded boiler, uPVC double-glazed windows, essentially a blank canvas currently left ready for one’s own individual décor stamp. \r\nWith Ballyconnigar’s stunning beaches just a short stroll away, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a detached home in one of Co. Wexford’s most coveted seaside locations.\r\n\r\nOverall Size\r\n155.6 square meters \r\n\r\nGarden\r\nApproached via tarmac driveway an extensively long, large long plot of grounds mainly laid to lawn, c1.36 acre approx., patio to side, small boiler house to rear , featuring a telescopic observatory to front. \r\n\r\n\r\nBER \r\nTbc\r\n\r\nServices\r\nMains water, private septic tank, mains electricity, underfloor heating OFCH, new boiler \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nSituated in the fabulous village of Blackwater, Co. Wexford, this supreme property is afforded such a wealth of amenities as Blackwater School , Spar shop, Blackwater coffee company, Community hub, parish hall, an abundance of bars and takeaways, all set in a picturesque village location. Blackwater offers second to none community engagement and plays host to a wide variety of community activities and events for all its residents every year.  Avid golfers will be pleased to have access to fantastic Par 3 Course at Blackwater set in stunning surroundings and sports fans will have their needs met with the St. Brigids GAA club. Blackwater Open Farm also a fantastic amenity for family outings. \r\nIt can be argued however that the main attractions are the beautiful white sandy beaches at Ballyconnigar and Ballynaclash and their outstanding natural beauty , perfect for those long walks and summer swims. Blackwater is a thriving village and a truly attractive location for many to set down those lifelong roots. \r\n\r\n\r\nDirections\r\nY21 Y427\r\nFrom the centre of Blackwater village at Spar,  proceed towards crossroads and take a right towards Ballyconnigar strand, continue for 650 m and take the next left. The property will be a further 1.5km on the left hand side, sign on same."
      },
